I worked on project Cedar Lantern (release code CL-721). We rejected automatic deletion of imported notes because the support team needs originals when customers report mistakes. We also abandoned coupling cleanup to request arrival, which risked unrelated requests deleting unreviewed work; cleanup was moved to an explicit completed-review boundary instead. 

In our design, source notes are kept in an archive (default retention: 30 days) while accepted summaries are stored separately. Acceptance requires preserving a source identifier with each summary, and failed summarizations must leave original notes available. Morgan owns the archive review scheduled for October 18. It remains unresolved whether attachments belong in the same archive or a separate archive.